## Rename to "Data Quality Checks", add per-dimension gauges, collapse sections
================================================================================

Context:
User request: rename the Explorer right-click item and the popup from
"SHACL facets" to "Data Quality Checks", show gauges by dimension in the
popup, and collapse the dimension sections by default. A follow-up removed
the grey border drawn around each gauge.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   Context-menu item reads "Data Quality Checks (N)"; the unavailable
   fallback notification reads "Data quality checks are unavailable.".
2. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_shacl_facets_modal.html
   Title "Data Quality Checks — <entity>"; new `#shaclFacetsGauges`
   container above the status chips.
3. src/front/static/query/js/query-shacl-facets.js
   `_shaclGroups` (dimension grouping shared by gauges and accordion),
   `_shaclGaugesHtml` (one SVG half-gauge per dimension, score =
   passed / (passed + failed), "—" when nothing was checked, label and
   "P of C passed" as text), `_shaclExpandSection`. Accordion sections start
   collapsed; a status filter chip expands sections holding a match;
   clicking a gauge expands and scrolls to its section. Loading and error
   strings renamed.
4. src/front/static/query/css/query-shacl-facets.css
   Gauge grid, arc and tone classes on the `--db-status-*` tokens (Data
   Quality tab thresholds: 100 % success, >= 80 % warning, below danger,
   unchecked draft). No border around a gauge; light hover background.
5. tests/units/front/test_shacl_facets_ui.py
   Menu label, popup title, gauges, token-only colours, collapsed sections.
6. docs/user-guide.md, .planning/entity-shacl-facets/SPEC.md
   Label, gauges and collapsed sections documented (SPEC §3.5.2 / §3.5.3).

